      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Numerous surgical procedures have been introduced to facilitate weight loss in morbidly obese individuals. Gastric reservoir reduction, wrapping the stomach with an inert fabric, is one such procedure. Nissen fundoplication has been performed in conjunction with this approach to prevent postoperative gastroesophageal reflux. Gastric perforation and functional gastroesophageal obstruction occurring as late as 71 months after this operation represent late complications. Perforation has developed in 14.6% of stomachs wrapped with polypropylene mesh. Nissen fundoplication may contribute to this complication."},
